4. Test the worm
Once you have written the code for your harmless worm, you can test it on a virtual machine or a computer that does not have any important data or applications running on it. This is to ensure that the worm does not accidentally cause any damage to the system or its applications.

5. Analyze the results
After running the worm on a test system, analyze the results to ensure that the worm did not cause any harm to the target computer or its applications. If everything looks good, then you have successfully created a harmless version of a worm for testing purposes.

